menu "bike_comm"

    choice BIKE_CODEC
        prompt "Voice codec"
        default BIKE_CODEC_LC3
        help
            Picks the voice codec compiled into the firmware. Both
            backends share the codec.h API (10 ms / 16 kHz / 40 B wire
            slot); only one is linked per build. See firmware/main/
            codec.h for the contract and docs/codec_perf.md for the
            measured LC3 numbers on LX6. Mesh peers must run matching
            builds — there is no on-air codec negotiation.

        config BIKE_CODEC_LC3
            bool "LC3 (google/liblc3, 32 kbps)"
            help
                Default. Vendored at firmware/components/liblc3/upstream.
                Bench-validated; this is what the v0 mesh runs on.

        config BIKE_CODEC_CODEC2
            bool "Codec2 3200 bps (drowe67/codec2) — STUB"
            help
                Build-time alternate for A/B speech eval and a future
                6-8-rider bandwidth fallback. 8 B per 20 ms padded into
                the 40 B wire slot every other tick. The upstream
                drowe67/codec2 source is NOT yet vendored — selecting
                this option compiles a stub that abort()s in codec_init
                with a clear log. Use to verify build wiring; do not
                flash for actual use until the upstream lands at
                firmware/components/codec2/upstream/ and codec_codec2.c
                grows past the stub.
    endchoice

endmenu
